# UX/UI Implementation Rules - Expert Guidelines

## 🎯 Implementation Philosophy

> "Write code as if the next person to maintain it is a violent psychopath who knows where you live."

### Core Principles:
1. **Consistency over creativity** - Follow existing patterns
2. **User feedback is king** - Always show loading, error, and empty states
3. **Performance first** - Every widget should be optimized
4. **Accessibility matters** - 15% of users have disabilities

## 🚨 MANDATORY Checks Before ANY UX/UI Change

### 1. Verify File Location
```bash
# WRONG PATH (common mistake):
lib/shared/widgets/empty_state_widget.dart

# CORRECT PATH:
lib/shared/widgets/states/empty_state_widget.dart
```

### 2. Check Imports Before Deleting
```bash
# ALWAYS run this before deleting any file:
grep -r "path/to/file" lib/
```

### 3. Run Analyze After Every Change
```bash
flutter analyze
# Fix ALL errors before proceeding
```

## 🎨 Theme Colors - NEVER Hardcode

### Light/Dark Mode Aware Colors:

| Hardcoded ❌ | Theme Color ✅ |
|-------------|----------------|
| `Colors.black` | `colorScheme.onSurface` |
| `Colors.white` | `colorScheme.surface` |
| `Colors.grey` | `colorScheme.outline` |
| `Colors.red` | `colorScheme.error` |
| `Colors.blue` | `colorScheme.primary` |
| `Colors.black12` | `colorScheme.shadow.withOpacity(0.1)` |

### Shadows in Dark Mode:
```dart
// ❌ Bad - visible shadow in dark mode
boxShadow: [BoxShadow(color: Colors.black26)]

// ✅ Good - no shadow in dark mode
boxShadow: Theme.of(context).brightness == Brightness.light
    ? [BoxShadow(color: Colors.black.withOpacity(0.1))]
    : null
```

## 📊 Three-State Pattern (MANDATORY for all data screens)

Every screen that displays data MUST handle:
1. ⏳ **Loading** - Show skeleton or spinner
2. ❌ **Error** - Show error with retry button
3. 📭 **Empty** - Show empty state with action button
4. ✅ **Data** - Show the actual content

```dart
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  final dataAsync = ref.watch(dataProvider);
  
  return dataAsync.when(
    loading: () => const LoadingWidget(useShimmer: true),
    error: (error, _) => ErrorStateWidget(
      message: error.toString(),
      onRetry: () => ref.invalidate(dataProvider),
    ),
    data: (items) {
      if (items.isEmpty) {
        return EmptyStateWidget(
          icon: Icons.inbox,
          message: 'No items yet',
          actionLabel: 'Add First Item',
          onAction: _showAddDialog,
        );
      }
      return _buildList(items);
    },
  );
}
```

## 🔄 RefreshIndicator Pattern

### For List Screens:
```dart
RefreshIndicator(
  onRefresh: () async {
    ref.invalidate(dataProvider);
    await ref.read(dataProvider.future);
  },
  child: ListView.builder(
    // CRITICAL: Enable pull even when empty
    physics: const AlwaysScrollableScrollPhysics(),
    cacheExtent: 500, // Performance optimization
    itemCount: items.length,
    itemBuilder: (context, index) => ItemCard(
      key: ValueKey(items[index].id),
      item: items[index],
    ),
  ),
)
```

## ⚡ Performance Optimizations

### 1. ListView Best Practices:
```dart
ListView.builder(
  // Performance optimizations
  cacheExtent: 500,          // Pre-render items ahead
  addAutomaticKeepAlives: false,  // Reduce memory
  addRepaintBoundaries: true,     // Reduce repaints
  
  // Enable pull-to-refresh on empty list
  physics: const AlwaysScrollableScrollPhysics(),
  
  // Use Keys for efficient rebuilds
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => KeyedSubtree(
    key: ValueKey(items[index].id),
    child: ItemCard(item: items[index]),
  ),
)
```

### 2. Provider Optimization:
```dart
// ❌ Bad - rebuilds on ANY account change
final account = ref.watch(accountProvider);

// ✅ Good - rebuilds only when balance changes
final balance = ref.watch(accountProvider.select((a) => a.balance));
```

### 3. const Constructors:
```dart
// ✅ ALWAYS use const for static widgets
const SizedBox(height: 16)
const EdgeInsets.all(16)
const Icon(Icons.add)
const Text('Title')
```

## 🔐 Context Safety After Async

### ALWAYS check context.mounted:
```dart
Future<void> _performAction() async {
  try {
    await ref.read(notifier).doSomething();
    
    // ✅ CRITICAL: Check before using context
    if (!context.mounted) return;
    
    FeedbackService.showSuccess(context, 'Done!');
    Navigator.pop(context);
    
  } catch (e) {
    // ✅ Also check in catch block
    if (!context.mounted) return;
    
    FeedbackService.showError(context, e.toString());
  }
}
```

## 📱 Touch Targets (Accessibility)

Minimum touch target size: **48x48 dp**

```dart
// ❌ Bad - Icon is only 24x24
Icon(Icons.add, size: 24)

// ✅ Good - Padding brings it to 48x48
Padding(
  padding: const EdgeInsets.all(12), // 24 + 12*2 = 48
  child: Icon(Icons.add, size: 24),
)

// ✅ Better - Use IconButton (48x48 default)
IconButton(
  icon: const Icon(Icons.add),
  onPressed: _onAdd,
  tooltip: 'Add item', // Also adds accessibility label
)
```

## 🌍 RTL Support

### Use Directional Properties:
```dart
// ❌ Wrong - doesn't flip in RTL
EdgeInsets.only(left: 16)
Alignment.centerLeft

// ✅ Correct - flips automatically in RTL
EdgeInsetsDirectional.only(start: 16)
AlignmentDirectional.centerStart
```

### Arrow Icons:
```dart
// ❌ Wrong - arrow points wrong way in RTL
Icon(Icons.arrow_forward)

// ✅ Correct - arrow respects text direction
Icon(Icons.arrow_forward_ios)
// Or use Directionality check:
Icon(Directionality.of(context) == TextDirection.rtl 
    ? Icons.arrow_back_ios 
    : Icons.arrow_forward_ios)
```

